**Wave 1** — now exploring, in parallel: Obtain the matter power spectrum ratio S(k) = P_hydro/P_DMO at z=0 over k = 0.1-10 h/Mpc for at least two feedback settings, a weak/fiducial one and a strong-ejection one. For each, report the depth of the minimum, the k at which the minimum occurs, and the k at which suppression first reaches 1%.; Explain the AGN feedback physics behind the suppression and bracket the predictions from different simulations. The explanation should cover gas ejection from group-scale haloes, the halo-mass dependence, the relation to baryon fraction, the effect of cooling at small scales, and the weak-versus-strong spread between simulations.; Assess the impact on weak-lensing cosmology. Cover the fractional change in cosmic-shear C_ell at ell~500-5000, the S8 bias that results if feedback is ignored, whether feedback can resolve the S8 tension, and constraints from joint WL+SZ analyses..
