[tool] d-01 post_finding {"claim": "Literature value (not computed): at z=0 the OWLS AGN model (van Daalen et al. 2011, arXiv:1104.1174) suppresses power relative to DMO by 1% at k~0.3 
[finding] f-001 Literature value (not computed): at z=0 the OWLS AGN model (van Daalen et al. 2011, arXiv:1104.1174) suppresses power relative to DMO by 1% at k~0.3 h/Mpc, 10% 
**Finding:** Literature value (not computed): at z=0 the OWLS AGN model (van Daalen et al. 2011, arXiv:1104.1174) suppresses power relative to DMO by 1% at k~0.3 h/Mpc, 10% at k~1 h/Mpc and 30% at k~10 h/Mpc. That gives k(1%)~0.3 h/Mpc, S(k=1)~0.90 and S(10)~0.70, with cooling dominant only at k>~70 h/Mpc. On this basis it serves as the strong, fiducial-AGN reference point.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-01-49 -> ok: Recorded finding f-001.
[tool] d-01 post_finding {"claim": "Literature (FLAMINGO, arXiv:2410.17109, not computed): the response gets stronger and its minimum moves to smaller scales as z falls. Lower cluster g
[finding] f-002 Literature (FLAMINGO, arXiv:2410.17109, not computed): the response gets stronger and its minimum moves to smaller scales as z falls. Lower cluster gas fraction
**Finding:** Literature (FLAMINGO, arXiv:2410.17109, not computed): the response gets stronger and its minimum moves to smaller scales as z falls. Lower cluster gas fractions and collimated jets (instead of thermal winds) strengthen the suppression. The strongest FLAMINGO models agree with some WL+external-data analyses but are in strong tension with X-ray cluster gas fractions. The GP emulator is accurate to 1% for k<10 h/Mpc and z<3. No numerical S_min or k_min values were extracted within the budget.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-01-50 -> ok: Recorded finding f-002.
