Title: Emulation of baryonic effects on the matter power spectrum and constraints
[usage]
[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794) model the non-linear power as P = P_L + A_mod(P_NL - P_L). With Planck LCDM fixed, a fit to KiDS-1000 cosmic she
[finding] f-003 Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794) model the non-linear power as P = P_L + A_mod(P_NL - P_L). With Planck LCDM fixed, a fit to KiDS-1000 cosmic shear needs A_
**Finding:** Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794) model the non-linear power as P = P_L + A_mod(P_NL - P_L). With Planck LCDM fixed, a fit to KiDS-1000 cosmic shear needs A_mod ~ 0.69, which is a suppression stronger than recent hydro simulations give. The tension being addressed is KiDS-1000 shear S8 = 0.759+0.024-0.021 and DES Y3 shear S8 = 0.772+0.018-0.017, against Planck S8 = 0.829+-0.012. That is about 9% (2.4-2.7 sigma) low for KiDS and about 7% (2.3-2.6 sigma) low for DES.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-03-52 -> ok: Recorded finding f-003.
[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827) find that DES Y3 cosmic shear needs a milder non-linear suppression than KiDS-1000 to agree with Planck
[finding] f-004 Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827) find that DES Y3 cosmic shear needs a milder non-linear suppression than KiDS-1000 to agree with Planck LCDM. It i
**Finding:** Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827) find that DES Y3 cosmic shear needs a milder non-linear suppression than KiDS-1000 to agree with Planck LCDM. It is still more extreme than recent simulations, and it must extend into the mildly non-linear regime, to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc. They name non-standard dark matter as an alternative cause. The DES best-fit A_mod value was not read in the sections examined.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-03-53 -> ok: Recorded finding f-004.
[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "FLAMINGO (McCarthy et al., arXiv:2309.07959) compares its full suite, including extreme feedback variants, with cosmic shear, CMB lensing, tSZ and th
[finding] f-005 FLAMINGO (McCarthy et al., arXiv:2309.07959) compares its full suite, including extreme feedback variants, with cosmic shear, CMB lensing, tSZ and their cross-s
**Finding:** FLAMINGO (McCarthy et al., arXiv:2309.07959) compares its full suite, including extreme feedback variants, with cosmic shear, CMB lensing, tSZ and their cross-spectra. It concludes that baryonic effects are not large enough to remove the S8 tension. Current cosmic shear data are only marginally sensitive to baryon physics. Stronger feedback improves the D3A-cosmology fit to KiDS/DES only slightly, and that preference largely goes away once a lower S8 is adopted. CMB lensing agrees well with Planck LCDM. The strongest tension comes from tSZ y-y, then shear x tSZ, then shear-shear.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-03-54 -> ok: Recorded finding f-005.
[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "Bigwood et al. (arXiv:2404.06098) fit DES Y3 WL + ACT DR5 kSZ with BCEmu baryonification. They get S8 = 0.823+0.019-0.020, higher than WL alone. The 
[finding] f-006 Bigwood et al. (arXiv:2404.06098) fit DES Y3 WL + ACT DR5 kSZ with BCEmu baryonification. They get S8 = 0.823+0.019-0.020, higher than WL alone. The fit prefers
**Finding:** Bigwood et al. (arXiv:2404.06098) fit DES Y3 WL + ACT DR5 kSZ with BCEmu baryonification. They get S8 = 0.823+0.019-0.020, higher than WL alone. The fit prefers a mean feedback scenario more extreme than most hydro simulations. At M500 ~ 1e13 Msun the baryon fraction comes out about 1.4 sigma below HSC-XXL X-ray. At M500 ~ 4e13 Msun, FLAMINGO predicts f_b about 1.5 sigma higher, MillenniumTNG about 3.1 sigma higher and FABLE about 1.4 sigma higher; BAHAMAS agrees best. They also state that model flexibility alone can shift S8 and degrade its error.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w1-d-03-55 -> ok: Recorded finding f-006.
