[tool] d-01 post_finding {"claim": "Literature (BCemu, Giri and Schneider, arXiv:2108.08863, not computed): fitting X-ray group and cluster gas fractions gives a z=0 suppression above t
[finding] f-007 Literature (BCemu, Giri and Schneider, arXiv:2108.08863, not computed): fitting X-ray group and cluster gas fractions gives a z=0 suppression above the percent 
**Finding:** Literature (BCemu, Giri and Schneider, arXiv:2108.08863, not computed): fitting X-ray group and cluster gas fractions gives a z=0 suppression above the percent level at k=0.1-0.4 h/Mpc (so k(1%) lies at 0.1-0.4 h/Mpc). The maximum suppression is 20-28% (S_min ~0.72-0.80) at k~7 h/Mpc, 68% CL. The OWLS-AGN value of 30% at k=10 h/Mpc sits just beyond the strong edge of this band. The FLAMINGO strongest jet and low-fgas models are stated to be in strong tension with X-ray gas fractions.
