[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "The abstracts give three more results. KiDS-1000 lensing x tSZ (arXiv:2109.04458, HMx) prefers strong feedback on its own and finds the amplitude sig
[finding] f-008 The abstracts give three more results. KiDS-1000 lensing x tSZ (arXiv:2109.04458, HMx) prefers strong feedback on its own and finds the amplitude sigma8(Om/0.3)
**Finding:** The abstracts give three more results. KiDS-1000 lensing x tSZ (arXiv:2109.04458, HMx) prefers strong feedback on its own and finds the amplitude sigma8(Om/0.3)^0.2 about 2 sigma low versus Planck; adding cosmic shear tightens S8 by 40% and gives feedback consistent with hydro simulations. DES Y3 harmonic-space shear (arXiv:2203.07128) finds S8 = 0.793+0.038-0.025 (1.5 sigma below Planck), and extending to k_max = 5 h/Mpc constrains feedback while leaving S8 essentially unchanged. OWLS-AGN (arXiv:1105.1075) shows that ignoring baryons biases w0 by about 40% for a Euclid-like survey; a calibrated halo model reduces this to about the statistical error.
