[finding] f-010 van Daalen+2019 (arXiv:1906.00968, 92 OWLS/cosmo-OWLS/BAHAMAS spectra): the large-scale suppression comes from feedback heating gas and ejecting it to large dis
**Finding:** van Daalen+2019 (arXiv:1906.00968, 92 OWLS/cosmo-OWLS/BAHAMAS spectra): the large-scale suppression comes from feedback heating gas and ejecting it to large distances, which is needed to match X-ray groups. An empirical model that uses only the mean baryon fraction in groups predicts the z=0 suppression to within 1% for k<1 h/Mpc, and differences in group baryon fraction explain the disagreement between simulations.
