[finding] f-011 van Loon and van Daalen 2023 (arXiv:2309.06479, cosmo-OWLS/BAHAMAS): AGN feedback ejects matter from inside r500c to r200m and possibly beyond in haloes with M5
**Finding:** van Loon and van Daalen 2023 (arXiv:2309.06479, cosmo-OWLS/BAHAMAS): AGN feedback ejects matter from inside r500c to r200m and possibly beyond in haloes with M500c>~1e13 Msun/h. For k<~3 h/Mpc, group-sized haloes (1e14+-0.25 Msun/h) dominate the power spectrum; at smaller scales the summed contribution of lower-mass haloes takes over. A lower AGN heating temperature damps the effect at k>~4 h/Mpc for M500c>=1e13.25. A parameter-free model built on halo baryon fractions reaches percent-level accuracy down to k~10 h/Mpc.
