[finding] f-012 Horizon-AGN (Chisari+2018, arXiv:1801.08559) is the weak end of the bracket: suppression at k~10 h/Mpc is <15% at z=0, with an enhancement of a factor of a few 
**Finding:** Horizon-AGN (Chisari+2018, arXiv:1801.08559) is the weak end of the bracket: suppression at k~10 h/Mpc is <15% at z=0, with an enhancement of a factor of a few at smaller scales from cooling and star formation. Its redshift evolution over z=0-5 is non-monotonic, and the authors conclude its AGN feedback is probably not strong enough.
