**Completed — Assess the impact on weak-lensing cosmology. Cover the fractional change in cosmic-shear C_ell at ell~500-5000, the S8 bias that results if feedback is ignored, whether feedback can resolve the S8 tension, and constraints from joint WL+SZ analyses..** Weak-lensing impact assessment (findings f-003 to f-006 and f-008). (1) Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794) model the power as P = P_L + A_mod(P_NL - P_L). Keeping Planck LCDM, KiDS-1000 shear needs A_mod ~ 0.69. The tension is KiDS shear S8 = 0.759+0.024-0.021 and DES Y3 shear S8 = 0.772+0.018-0.017 against Planck S8 = 0.829+-0.012: about 9% (2.4-2.7 sigma) and 7% (2.3-2.6 sigma) low. (2) Preston et al. (arXiv:2305.09827): DES Y3 needs milder suppression than KiDS but still more than the simulations give, and it must reach down to k~0.2 h/Mpc. The DES best-fit A_mod value was not extracted. (3) FLAMINGO (arXiv:2309.07959): even its extreme feedback variants are too weak to remove the tension. Current shear data are only marginally sensitive to baryons, and the slight preference for stronger feedback in the D3A cosmology fades once a lower S8 is adopted. The strongest tension is in tSZ y-y, then shear x tSZ, then shear-shear. (4) DES Y3 WL + ACT kSZ (arXiv:2404.06098): S8 = 0.823+0.019-0.020, with feedback more extreme than most simulations. f_b at M500~1e13 Msun is about 1.4 sigma below X-ray; FLAMINGO, MTNG and FABLE predict f_b 1.5, 3.1 and 1.4 sigma higher at about 4e13 Msun, and BAHAMAS agrees best. (5) KiDS x tSZ (arXiv:2109.04458): the cross-correlation alone prefers strong feedback and is about 2 sigma low; adding shear tightens S8 by 40% and gives feedback consistent with simulations. DES Y3 harmonic space (arXiv:2203.07128): S8 = 0.793+0.038-0.025 at 1.5 sigma, and k_max = 5 h/Mpc leaves S8 essentially unchanged. OWLS-AGN (arXiv:1105.1075): about 40% w0 bias for Euclid if baryons are ignored. Verdict: simulation-calibrated feedback (FLAMINGO) cannot resolve the tension. Resolving it needs A_mod-type suppression reaching k~0.2 h/Mpc, beyond what the simulations give; only the WL+kSZ fit prefers such extreme feedback, and the X-ray gas fractions and FLAMINGO argue against it. Gaps: I did not extract a quoted S8 shift in sigma from ignoring feedback for DES/KiDS, the fractional C_ell change at ell 500-5000, or the numerical suppression at k=0.2-1 h/Mpc implied by A_mod=0.69. Full texts are in runs/261017_110039/*.txt, and no cite() entries were added.
