**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 0 findings stand up to the evidence, 13 questioned ('Literature value (not computed): at z=0 the OWLS AGN model (van Daalen et al. 2011, arXiv:': The quoted excerpt from tc-d-01-38 contains only the title, authors and header of arXiv:1104.1174. None of the claimed values (1% at k~0.3, 10% at k~1, 30% at k~10 h/Mpc, cooling at k>~70) appears in the quoted text. The abstract sentence needs to be quoted verbatim. Calling OWLS AGN the 'strong' reference also conflicts with d-02, which places it as intermediate.; 'Literature (FLAMINGO, arXiv:2410.17109, not computed): the response gets stronger and its ': The excerpt from tc-d-01-36 is header-only. None of these claims is shown: response strengthening as z decreases, the minimum moving to smaller scales, stronger suppression with jets and low fgas, tension with X-ray gas fractions, and 1% emulator accuracy.; 'Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794) model the non-linear power as P = P_L + A_mod(P_NL - ': Both excerpts (tc-d-03-33, -35) stop at the abstract heading. A_mod~0.69 and the KiDS/DES/Planck S8 values with their sigma levels are not in the quoted text. The percentage-low and sigma figures also look derived rather than quoted, and their provenance is not stated.; 'Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827) find that DES Y3 cosmic shear needs a milder': The excerpt from tc-d-03-35 is header-only. The 'milder than KiDS' result, the extension to k~0.2 h/Mpc and the non-standard dark matter alternative are not shown.).

Issues: The core task was to use emulator tools to predict S(k) at z=0 for two parameter points, and this was not done. Every number is a literature read, and even those lack verbatim support. The task is unanswered on its primary quantitative deliverable.; Feedback strength is labelled inconsistently. d-01 calls OWLS AGN the strong/fiducial reference, while d-02 calls it intermediate. The weak/strong pair (q-02) is still undefined, so the S_min/k_min table has no clear rows.; The strong end of the bracket is empty: there are no FLAMINGO jet, BAHAMAS high-AGN or WL+kSZ S(k=1) or S_min values. Astrid (no suppression at z=0) and TNG are cited only through board summaries and have no findings..
