[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "Verbatim from Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794, Eq. 7): with the cosmology fixed to Planck TTTEEE LCDM, the KiDS-1000 xi_pm fit gives \"a mean Amo
[finding] f-014 Verbatim from Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794, Eq. 7): with the cosmology fixed to Planck TTTEEE LCDM, the KiDS-1000 xi_pm fit gives "a mean Amod = 0.69 ± 0
**Finding:** Verbatim from Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2206.11794, Eq. 7): with the cosmology fixed to Planck TTTEEE LCDM, the KiDS-1000 xi_pm fit gives "a mean Amod = 0.69 ± 0.06" with chi2_min = 265.5 for 225 data points. The authors note that this uncertainty is underestimated because it neglects the Planck cosmology error. HMCode2020 with a broad prior instead gives Theta_AGN = 9.17+0.2-0.8, well outside the BAHAMAS-calibrated range 7.6-8.0. The paper states that "the power spectrum suppression required to reconcile the KiDS cosmic shear measurements with the Planck cosmology is more extreme than predicted by most of the hydrodynamic simulations" (Fig. 6). For KiDS, ignoring feedback (HMCode2020 no feedback) gives S8 = 0.755+-0.016, against 0.774+-0.021 for the fiducial Theta_AGN = 7.3-8.3 prior (Table 1): a shift of about 0.02, roughly 1 sigma.
[tool] tc-261017_1-w2-d-06-96 -> ok: Recorded finding f-014.
[tool] d-06 post_finding {"claim": "Verbatim from Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827). With a Planck prior and no scale cuts, DES Y3 gives \"Amod = 0.858 \u00b1 0.052\", which
[finding] f-015 Verbatim from Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827). With a Planck prior and no scale cuts, DES Y3 gives "Amod = 0.858 ± 0.052", which differs from unit
**Finding:** Verbatim from Preston, Amon & Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827). With a Planck prior and no scale cuts, DES Y3 gives "Amod = 0.858 ± 0.052", which differs from unity by about 2.7 sigma (Eq. 3). KiDS reanalysed with the same Planck prior gives Amod = 0.748 ± 0.072, about 1 sigma above the 0.69 of Paper I (Eq. 5). The naive combination is Amod = 0.820 ± 0.042 for DES Y3 + KiDS, meaning suppression is required at about 4 sigma (Eq. 6). Over k <~ 1 h/Mpc, BAHAMAS log10(dT_heat/K) = 8.0 "is well approximated by Amod = 0.9". The required suppression is stronger than that, closer to C-OWLS 8.5/8.7, and must extend to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc (Fig. 2 right, Fig. 6). On S8 when baryons are ignored: DES Y3 with no scale cuts and no feedback (variant 4) gives S8 = 0.793 ± 0.012, which is 1.8 sigma below Planck TTTEEE 0.828 ± 0.016. With scale cuts (variant 3) it gives 0.805 ± 0.017, 0.9 sigma below. Adding Amod with free cosmology (variant 5) gives 0.831 ± 0.036 (Table 2). Removing the baryon-feedback mitigation therefore lowers DES S8 by about 0.04 relative to the Amod-free fit, which is about 1 sigma of that fit.
