[finding] f-020 FLAMINGO strong end versus data (arXiv:2410.17109), verbatim: 'both fgas−8σ models (i.e. with thermal AGN and with collimated jet AGN) are within the ranges dem
**Finding:** FLAMINGO strong end versus data (arXiv:2410.17109), verbatim: 'both fgas−8σ models (i.e. with thermal AGN and with collimated jet AGN) are within the ranges demanded by the analysis of Bigwood et al. 2024 (with or without added kSZ constraints)', yet they 'display gas fractions that are in strong tension with the gas fractions in groups and clusters inferred from joint X-ray and weak-lensing analyses (Kugel et al. 2023)'. Also: the Amon & Efstathiou (2022) response and, to a lesser extent, the Preston et al. (2023) response 'are out of reach of our emulator and likely of what can be achieved using the FLAMINGO model without altering the sub-grid models'.
