[direction] d-06 -> closed
**Completed — Give the weak-lensing assessment quoted numbers. Obtain verbatim support for A_mod~0.69 (KiDS) and the DES Y3 A_mod best fit from 2206.11794 and 2305.09827. Find any quoted suppression at k=0.2-1 h/Mpc, any fractional change in C_ell, or any S8 shift in sigma attributable to ignoring baryons, and quote the FLAMINGO 2309.07959 conclusion that feedback cannot resolve the tension..** Partly done: the A_mod quotes and the S8 shifts are now verbatim, but there is no fractional C_ell change, no suppression number at k=0.2-1 h/Mpc, no FLAMINGO quote from this round and no cite() entries.

1. KiDS (Amon and Efstathiou, arXiv:2206.11794, Eq. 7; finding f-014): with the cosmology fixed to Planck, "a mean Amod = 0.69 ± 0.06", chi2_min = 265.5 for 225 data points. The authors say this error is underestimated because it leaves out the Planck cosmology error. The HMCode2020 version of the fit needs Theta_AGN = 9.17+0.2-0.8 (Eq. 8), well outside the BAHAMAS-calibrated range of 7.6-8.0. The paper says the required suppression is "more extreme than predicted by most of the hydrodynamic simulations" (Fig. 6). From Table 1, S8 for KiDS is 0.755+-0.016 with feedback switched off and 0.774+-0.021 with the fiducial Theta_AGN 7.3-8.3 prior, a shift of about 0.02 (about 1 sigma).

2. DES Y3 (Preston, Amon and Efstathiou, arXiv:2305.09827; finding f-015): with a Planck prior and no scale cuts, Amod = 0.858 ± 0.052, which is 2.7 sigma from 1 (Eq. 3). KiDS refit with the same Planck prior gives Amod = 0.748 ± 0.072 (Eq. 5). Combining the two gives Amod = 0.820 ± 0.042, so suppression is needed at about 4 sigma (Eq. 6). Over k <~ 1 h/Mpc, BAHAMAS with heating parameter 8.0 is approximated by Amod = 0.9. The data need more suppression than that, close to the C-OWLS 8.5/8.7 runs, and it must reach k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc (abstract; Fig. 2 right, Fig. 6).

3. S8 shift from ignoring baryons (Table 2 of 2305.09827): with all scales used and no feedback, DES gives S8 = 0.793 ± 0.012, 1.8 sigma below Planck TTTEEE (0.828 ± 0.016). With scale cuts it gives 0.805 ± 0.017, 0.9 sigma below. With Amod and free cosmology it gives 0.831 ± 0.036. So leaving out the suppression lowers S8 by about 0.04, roughly 1 sigma of the Amod fit.

Not found (dead end x-02): neither paper gives a fractional C_ell or xi_+ change at ell 500-5000, or an S(k) number at k=0.2-1 h/Mpc, in the text I read (2206.11794 characters 0-46000, 2305.09827 characters 0-42000). The suppression appears only in figures (2206.11794 Fig. 6; 2305.09827 Figs. 2, 4, 6), and both papers work with xi_pm rather than C_ell.

FLAMINGO (2309.07959): not re-read in this round. The conclusion that feedback is too weak to remove the S8 tension still rests only on finding f-005.

No cite() entries were added. Texts used: /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-baryonic-pk/runs/261017_110039/2206.11794.txt and 2305.09827.txt.

Still open: a verbatim quote from the 2309.07959 conclusions, and cite() entries for 2206.11794, 2305.09827 and 2309.07959.
