**Blocked — Fix the contested evidence and fill the strong end of the simulation bracket. Obtain verbatim quotes for the key numbers in 1104.1174 (OWLS), 2410.17109 (FLAMINGO jet and low-fgas variants, S(k=1) and S_min) and 2605.04176 (Astrid). Use these to build a weak-to-strong bracket of S(k=1) and S_min at z=0..** (Two things are missing. First, numerical S(k=1) and S_min for FLAMINGO's fgas-8sigma and jet models appear only in plots (Figs. 5, 6, 11 and 13 of 2410.17109), never in the text; getting them means extracting those figures and reading values off the curves. Second, the tool budget ran out before cite() was called, so references.bib has no entries yet for 2410.17109 or 2605.04176, and the 1104.1174 quote is not re-cited. Dead end x-04 records this.) This direction is partly done. I quoted the three papers verbatim from their full texts and posted the results as f-018 to f-021. The strong end of the bracket is placed by the papers' own statements, but the text gives no numerical S(k=1) or S_min for FLAMINGO's strong models, so that success criterion is not met. All values are at z=0.

Bracket, weak to strong:
(1) Astrid (arXiv:2605.04176, f-021) is the weak end. Abstract: 'no significant suppression at z = 0 and mild suppression at z = 0.2, weaker than in other state-of-the-art simulations'. Text: at z=0.2 mild suppression extends to k~1 h/Mpc, then the ratio 'rises back to above unity at z = 0'. So S(k=1) is about 1 or above, with no S_min below 1. The relevant figure is Fig. 1.
(2) Horizon-AGN (arXiv:1801.08559, f-012 from d-02): less than 15% suppression at k~10 h/Mpc. That excerpt was not re-quoted here.
(3) FLAMINGO fiducial (arXiv:2410.17109, f-019): the minimum is at k=10 h/Mpc and the ratio first departs from unity at k~0.1 h/Mpc. For the thermal gas-fraction variants the minimum stays at k=8-10 h/Mpc.
(4) OWLS AGN (arXiv:1104.1174, f-018) is labelled intermediate. Abstract: suppression of 1% at k~0.3, 10% at k~1 and 30% at k~10 h/Mpc, so S(k=1)~0.90 and S(k=10)~0.70.
(5) FLAMINGO strong-end variants (f-019, f-020): the jet model gives a larger response than the thermal model at the same gas-fraction setting. The thermal and jet versions of the model whose cluster gas fractions sit 8 sigma below the calibration data ('fgas-8sigma') 'closely resemble' cosmo-OWLS with AGN heating temperature log ΔT = 8.3 and 8.5. The thermal response stops growing below that setting. Both are 'within the ranges demanded' by Bigwood+2024 but 'in strong tension' with X-ray/WL gas fractions. The Amon & Efstathiou response is 'out of reach' of FLAMINGO. Only Illustris and cosmo-OWLS ΔT = 8.7 lie beyond the emulator's range. The relevant figures are Figs. 2, 5, 6, 11 and 13 of 2410.17109.

