Issues: The task explicitly asks for emulator-predicted Pk-ratios at z=0 for a couple of parameter points. No emulator was run, and no S(k=1) or S(k=5) value exists for any named parameter point. The final report must state plainly that every S(k) value is a literature value. An analytic stand-in may still be possible: the SP(k) or van Daalen+2019 fitting formulae evaluated by hand from published coefficients. That route has not been tried.; The evidence excerpts show only the first few hundred characters of 10,000-16,000 character text chunks. None of the quoted claim strings is actually visible in the excerpts: the Amod = 0.69 +- 0.06 quote, the 21-28% band, the FLAMINGO 'closely resemble' sentence and the Astrid 'rises back to above unity' sentence. I accepted these findings because the chunk ranges plausibly cover the cited sections (abstracts at chars 0-4000, Sec. 4 later in the text) and the quotes are internally consistent with earlier findings. Future findings should store the exact matching snippet as the excerpt.; f-018 ranks OWLS AGN as 'stronger than FLAMINGO fiducial'. No quoted number supports this, because the FLAMINGO fiducial S(k=1) and S_min are not given in the text. The only support is the OWLS 10% at k~1. The ordering against Horizon-AGN is also loose: Horizon-AGN gives under 15% at k~10, while OWLS gives 30% at k~10. Treat the ranking as provisional..
